1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,284
How much thermal paste should you use?

2
00:00:02,564 --> 00:00:04,203
Less than you probably think.

3
00:00:04,953 --> 00:00:09,867
Thermal paste fills the microscopic gaps between your processor and its cooler.

4
00:00:10,147 --> 00:00:14,090
Air is a terrible conductor of heat, and the paste pushes it out.

5
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:19,190
The common advice is a dot about the size of a pea, right in the middle.

6
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:22,174
When you mount the cooler, the pressure spreads it out.

7
00:00:22,924 --> 00:00:24,533
Too little leaves air gaps.

8
00:00:24,813 --> 00:00:29,472
Too much just squeezes out the sides and makes a mess, without cooling any better.

9
00:00:30,222 --> 00:00:31,758
And check your cooler first.

10
00:00:32,038 --> 00:00:36,119
Many come with paste already applied, so you may not need any extra.

11
00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:38,965
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

